 ### Haze and volumetrics
 
-`RtxNumos::beginFrame` resolves the exclusivity once per frame, after the weather is blended. It never writes an option.
+At frame begin the device resolves the Enhanced `volumetrics` policy and the player's Remix fog switch. Value 0 pauses the froxel passes. Value 1 with Remix fog enabled bounds its medium to the camera's froxel range and passes that world-space distance to NUMOS as `volumetricsHandoffWorldUnits`. The library integrates its near field and light glow starting at that distance. The composite puts Remix light in front of the NUMOS air. With the player's switch off, value 1 uses the full NUMOS haze.
 
-While volumetrics are on, it clears `aerialPerspective` and `fogVisibilityMeters` in the settings that go to the renderer. The height fog needs its own clear, because the cloud composite applies it independently of aerial perspective. The distance haze of the clouds comes from the cloud march, which depends on neither setting. `volumetricsHandoffWorldUnits` stays 0, because the two never share a range.
+Value 2 keeps the original rule. While the player's switch is on, the adapter clears `aerialPerspective` and `fogVisibilityMeters` in the frame settings. Cloud distance haze is part of the cloud march. All three policies leave the player's saved options alone.
 
 `skyHazeActive` needs aerial perspective, no dome light, and a camera outside of media. While it is set, every `calculateFog` site is skipped.
 
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@ While volumetrics are on, it clears `aerialPerspective` and `fogVisibilityMeters
 | The rest of a PSR pixel, and inactive sparse PSR pixels | The PSR surface |
 | Miss | The air up to the sky |
 
-A miss never gets the depth based fog, which would paint over the sky. The froxel radiance cache still runs while the haze is on, because other systems read it.
+A miss skips the depth-based fog. In the paused policy, surface consumers see empty Remix radiance resources. Resuming creates fresh froxel histories.
 
